\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Mexican peso strong, but not stronger than Colombian  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Most emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have gained ground during the first seven months of the year against the US dollar, with the Colombian peso and the Mexican peso being the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that have appreciated the most, but the context of this appreciation between the two Latin American countries is explained differently. So far this year, the Colombian peso has appreciated 17.3%; the Mexican peso, 12.8%; the Brazilian real, 9.2%; the Chilean peso, 6.9%; the Hungarian forint, 6.7%; the Polish zloty, 6.6%; and the Peruvian sol, 4.8%.\par \par \uc2 Why is the Mexican peso strong? During the semester, the Mexican peso appreciated 12.8% and is already close to breaking the level of 17 units per dollar, due to the timely \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  to control inflation since June 2021, according to analysts. The differential between Mexico's rate and that of the United States has generated an attraction for peso assets, in addition, record levels of remittances and the attraction of investment have supported the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Gabriela Siller, director of economic analysis at Banco Base, mentioned that the fact that the peso remains strong raises the probability that the exchange rate will continue to show a downward trend. In fact, if the exchange rate shows the same trend observed since July of last year, this 2023 could reach a minimum quotation of 16.74 pesos. "The strength of the peso is not due to the government's economic policy, it is due to the flow of dollars coming in from exports, remittances and foreign direct investment, in addition to the monetary policy of \uc2 Banco de M\u233\'00\'E9xico\uc2  and the preference of foreigners to invest in pesos. What has helped the current administration is that the autonomy of the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  has been respected and the investment grade of the sovereign debt has not been lost. Plus the factor that the golden opportunity of nearshoring has appeared, which implies a greater flow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to Mexico", added Siller. What about Colombia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? The appreciation of the Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to internal and external factors. On the domestic side, the political climate has had an influence, as \uc2 Gustavo Petro\uc2 's government's reform proposals on labor, pension and health issues have encountered many debates and obstacles in Congress, which sends a signal of confidence to the market regarding the autonomy of the country's institutions. On the external side, the strength of the Colombian peso has been influenced by a greater appetite for emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , due to the expectation that central banks, especially the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , may end its restrictive policy. "When the idea that there will be no more interest rate hikes and that external agents have a little more appetite for risk is consolidated, surely capital will continue to arrive to the Colombian economy but not in the same way as it was seen at the beginning of the year; in such a way that not much appreciation of the exchange rate is expected but not much depreciation either, since the markets are calmer and above all inflation and interest rates in the world are ceasing to rise", \uc2 Scotiabank Colpatria\uc2  analysts indicated in a report. One Colombian peso to one Mexican peso The exchange rate conversion between these Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is one Mexican peso for 242.81 Colombian pesos. Conversely, for one Colombian peso you would be paying 0.0041 Mexican pesos.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230706ej7600bpz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
