\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Mexican peso declines on Fed officials'  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 220 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Februar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Feb 8 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso depreciated on Wednesday, but continued to hover below the barrier of 19 per dollar, in a market awaiting the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of several officials of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  in the course of the day.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 18.9264 units, with a loss of 0.27%, as investors continued to evaluate comments from the head of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2 , who showed in a speech on Tuesday few signs of an aggressive stance on the strength of employment.\par \par \uc2 "During the session, the performance of the exchange market will depend mainly on comments from \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  officials," the firm Banco Base said in an analysis note.\par \par \uc2 Speeches were scheduled throughout the day by \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  President \uc2 John Williams\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Lisa Cook, \uc2 Atlanta Fed\uc2  President \uc2 Raphael Bostic\uc2  and \uc2 Minneapolis Fed\uc2  chief Neel Kaskari, among others.\par \par \uc2 Investors' attention was also focused on Thursday's release of local inflation figures for January and on \uc2 Banco de M\u233\'00\'E9xico\uc2 's first monetary policy announcement of the year.\par \par \uc2 For the time being, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to oscillate the rest of the day in a range of 18.81 to 18.95 per dollar, according to analysts at CI Banco.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230209ej2