\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Mexico is well positioned to weather the risks of a turbulent global environment: \uc2 IMF\b0\par\par\uc2 564 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) considered that Mexico is well positioned to weather the risks of the turbulent global environment, which has been generated by inflation, high interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation.\par \par \uc2 "Faced with increased risks in a more turbulent global environment, the (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) Directors agreed that Mexico is well positioned to weather the challenges, due to the soundness of its macroeconomic policies and economic policy frameworks," informed the \uc2 Bank of Mexico (Banxico)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that the Executive Directors agreed with the thrust of the \uc2 IMF\uc2  staff's assessment of the Mexican economy in 2022.\par \par \uc2 They also welcomed the authorities' prudent macroeconomic policies in the face of a rebound in inflation, according to the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 's annual assessment of the Mexican economy in 2022, which was published by \uc2 Banxico\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2  evaluates the economic situation and outlook of each of the Fund's member countries, generally on an annual basis.\par \par \uc2 As part of the assessment, an \uc2 IMF\uc2  staff team visits the member country, collects and analyzes economic and financial information, and meets with the relevant authorities, as well as with private sector analysts and representatives of civil society.\par \par \uc2 The issues reviewed are not limited to macroeconomic and financial policies, but also include those elements that may have an impact on a country's economic performance.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 IMF\uc2 's assessment expects Mexico's economic growth to slow in the short term due to slower U.S. growth and tighter global financial conditions.\par \par \uc2 "Directors welcomed the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 's proactive approach to dealing with rising inflation," explains the document published by the body led by Victoria Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Ceja.\par \par \uc2 Given the significant uncertainty about the inflation trajectory in 2023 and upside risks, \uc2 IMF\uc2  Directors agreed that further increases in the target rate and the maintenance of a tight policy stance for some time in Mexico may be necessary.\par \par \uc2 They also generally stressed the importance of clear communication of economic policy.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  Directors recommended aligning wage increases more closely with expected inflation and the productivity of lower-paid workers, as well as the neutral fiscal stance planned for 2022 and 2023 is appropriate.\par \par \uc2 "The easing of retail fuel prices (in Mexico), while reducing cost pressures, came at a considerable cost to the budget and, in general, they urged the authorities to choose more targeted supports to protect other priority spending in the event that oil prices rise again," the \uc2 IMF\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 It added that contingency plans should be prepared for a rapid policy response should downside risks materialize.\par \par \uc2 "It would be important to increase fiscal buffers in the short term and reform the institutional framework for greater flexibility in the longer term," it added.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  Directors noted that the floating exchange rate in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  should continue to act as a buffer, although \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market could be considered should there be a significant worsening of market liquidity.\par \par \uc2 They agreed that the financial system remains resilient post-pandemic, welcomed the favorable assessment of the effectiveness of Mexico's financial stability framework, and generally supported the key policy recommendations of the 2022 Financial Sector Assessment Program (FSAP).\par \par \uc2 "Additional measures, including an update of the financial sector supervisory and crisis management frameworks, are needed to keep pace with a changing regulatory and risk landscape," they concluded.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221104eib400bon\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
