\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 AMLO vs. \uc2 Banxico\uc2 , stability hurts; KREO for mortgages in other countries\b0\par\par\uc2 569 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 All was well at the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 , despite its historic decision to raise its benchmark rate. The Bank of Mexico's decision to raise rates by 75 basis points, the largest increase since the target rate has been in place, was well received by the market. It was taken as a firm commitment by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lower inflation. Even the Mexican peso reacted well, trading better against the dollar. However, there was one voice that did not like the decision, and that was President \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The President took the opportunity of his morning press conference to criticize the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He said he respected the autonomy of the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 , but raising the interest rate as the only measure to lower inflation seemed unimaginative. "Central bankers are technicians and feel they are scientists".\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  there must be other mechanisms to lower inflation, and there are other mechanisms to lower it, but they do not depend on the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends on its monetary policy, that is, the interest rate. And the interest rate hike did imply a commitment from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Victoria Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Ceja, governor of \uc2 Banco de \b \highlight22\uc2 M\u233\'00\'E9xico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , explained to us that they seek to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in price formation, in expectations. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision took into account the complexity of the environment (imported inflation, upward pressure from the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 ). And he is right.\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  cannot demand much more from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . To lower inflation there are other factors that do not depend on the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 , such as productivity and sectoral policies and, of course, that the government keeps its finances healthy.\par \par \uc2 Did it bother the President that the deputy governors and governor proposed by him(Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez Ceja, \uc2 Jonathan Heath\uc2 , \uc2 Gerardo Esquivel\uc2 , Galia Borja) voted for the rate hike? Who knows. What is certain is that the Board of Governors did the right thing in maintaining its autonomy and upholding its constitutional mandate to preserve the purchasing value of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MORTGAGES ABROAD, HOW TO GET RID OF FEAR?\par \par \uc2 Mortgage brokers are useful. They are advisors. They review your case, your income, your needs. They make you a tailor-made suit, through a bank with your best mortgage credit option. One of those brokers, the largest in the country, is KREO.\par \par \uc2 KREO, headed by Eugenio Klee and Francisco Y\u225\'00\'E1\u241\'00\'F1ez, today takes an interesting step: they present their global strategy, and through them Mexicans will be able to obtain a mortgage in other countries. They will tell you the steps to take, and will help you obtain a mortgage in the United States, Canada, Spain or Portugal. They have partners there, and it is similar to here: they analyze your possibilities.\par \par \uc2 The brokers do not charge commission. They work with the banks. And today, with the creation of KREO Global, you will have access to banks, for example, in the US, with rates of around 5% per year to buy in Houston, San Antonio, Austin or Dallas. Or for example in Spain, in cities such as Madrid, Seville or Salamanca, where the mortgage rate is 1.5%; or Portugal or Canada.\par \par \uc2 There is an appetite among Mexicans who, without being millionaires, want to take out a mortgage loan in another country. KREO is targeting this market.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220627ei6r0030n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
