\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The West vs. Russia\b0\par\par\uc2 1,255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 To Ian, for sharing his knowledge\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Proceso) -At the beginning of the year I wrote in Proceso about the beginning of a new Cold War due to the tension between Russia and Ukraine. I alluded to the political division of the world for several decades. The polarization is now between Europe and Russia, but it is a game in which the United States has the final word. What I did not imagine is that it would not become a conventional war between two countries, but the war of all Western countries against Russia. Ukraine aroused a unanimity that I do not recall had ever been reached.\par \par \uc2 The regrettable US invasion of Iraq in 2003, far from provoking an outcry over the senselessness of a war that would soon cause more than 1 million deaths, hundreds of thousands of wounded and maimed, millions of displaced persons and refugees in other countries, was supported by England, Germany, Spain and other countries, which now condemn Russia's incursion into Ukraine whose damage so far is not comparable.\par \par \uc2 No action of war is justifiable, but the unanimity aroused with the leadership of the United States, whose president, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , thus resorts to distraction about his inability to govern his country, is strange. His interference in other countries has been demonstrated by the disasters he has left in Iraq and Afghanistan, but there are also the sanctions with serious social consequences. It has done so on more than 115 occasions (1918-1998), 64 of which occurred in the 1990s. And in 1997 alone, half of the world's population suffered from its sanctions (H\u233\'00\'E9l\u232\'00\'E8ne Richard and Anne-C\u233\'00\'E9cile Robert, Le Monde Diplomatique, March 2022). There are also the trade embargoes on Kuwait, Syria and Lebanon regardless of the famine and deaths.\par \par \uc2 What had happened before February 24 when Russia advanced on Ukraine? In 1991 the Soviet Union was dissolved. Since 1997, \uc2 NATO\uc2  has given accession to several countries of Eastern Europe and the former Soviet Union. George Kenan, the renowned diplomat who contributed to the d\u233\'00\'E9tente between the United States and Russia, said: "\uc2 NATO\uc2  enlargement is the most fatal mistake in U.S. foreign policy since the end of the Cold War".\par \par \uc2 In 2014 in Minsk, the capital of Belarus, the protocol was signed to ease the tension in eastern Ukraine and cease its attacks in Donetsk and Luganks, a war that reached 10,000 victims. In 2015 Minsk was reactivated with the signatures of Germany, France, Russia and Ukraine, but peace was never fully established and in the Donbas area fighting continued. On February 22, Russia recognized the independence of these regions, which it had encouraged. President Volodymir Zelensky criticized the Western allies for leaving Ukraine alone because he did not want to lose those regions, although he did not achieve peace.\par \par \uc2 Russia had already asked \uc2 NATO\uc2  to stop its eastward expansion, to withdraw Western troops from the new countries and to repatriate deployed nuclear weapons. The opposite happened, because military-technical cooperation with Ukraine was intensified. Obviously, its entry and the possible installation of nuclear bases of the Western countries and the United States were sponsored. The objective was to encircle Russia and Putin used the image that for Russia it was the same as if Russia were to place bases in Mexico. This was reminiscent of the missile crisis in 1962, when it tried to establish bases in Cuba.\par \par \uc2 The crisis has favored Ukraine by opening the doors to \uc2 NATO\uc2 , despite the previous commitment of the United States to avoid it, and it will also be able to accede to the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . The situation is reversed when Ukraine appears as the beneficiary of the Russian incursion. Why is it that what seemed to be a Russian strategy for non-explicit purposes turns against it and is slammed by the Western countries that allow the United States to regain its hegemonic position as leader of the West?\par \par \uc2 Russia is condemned by all. Biden haughtily affirms that Putin will be punished for his aggression. The head of \uc2 NATO\uc2  accuses him of destroying peace in Europe. Countries agree to criticize it in the most extreme manner. The resources denied to alleviate humanitarian crises magically appear and Ukraine receives millions of euros to buy high-powered weapons and even machine guns distributed among civilian militias.\par \par \uc2 Europe and other countries seem to have no memory as they join the unanimous narrative with a single perspective, that of the official voice to not only bend Russia but to humiliate it. And then comes the most severe sanction since the globality that allows, with the use of the swift, to deprive the country of its monetary reserves, preventing the use of 640 billion dollars frozen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The banks of New York, London and even Switzerland have been closed for the Russians, in contravention of the political neutrality maintained even during the Second World War. 268 billion dollars have been frozen for private companies in Russian foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  banks, as well as 400 billion dollars invested in Russia. \uc2 Citizens\uc2  are unable to dispose of their 12 trillion euro cash and must stand in endless lines to get some of their own savings. They are betting that the ruble will collapse -it has already fallen several points- and the recession will provoke distrust and even an uprising like those designed by the United States to bring down governments in other countries.\par \par \uc2 Russia is losing the economic war and is also humiliated with numerous actions. Unanimity was expressed at the \uc2 UN\uc2  when the Russian Foreign Minister, Serguei Lavrov, when speaking, the room was abandoned by 100 delegations, depriving them of hearing another argumentation. Why, if his judgment has already been pronounced. Zelensky also wins the majority support of the \uc2 European Parliament\uc2  for Ukraine's accession to the \uc2 European Union\uc2  because "we are fighting for the freedom you have".\par \par \uc2 Russia has to be put down and it does not matter if traditions and ways of acting towards others are set aside, and the Hague Tribunal is already preparing to prosecute it for war crimes, when denunciations of other nations have been disdained for years. FIFA, breaking what kept it above politics, has deprived Russia of all its powers. So have other supposedly sporting organizations. In addition, \uc2 Apple\uc2  has decided not to sell its products in Russia. Film companies will not exhibit their films. The Cannes Film Festival has announced that it will not accept the participation of Russian productions. In the extreme, a ban on the purchase of scientific inputs and products is being induced. And despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on non-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it has suspended the Sputnik vaccine that was being applied. But that's not all, because Putin himself must suffer the humiliation and, although it makes one laugh, the International Taekwondo Organization has withdrawn his black belt.\par \par \uc2 All this looks like a program from the old TV series The Twilight Zone, because only one language is spoken and nobody listens to another. In the past different opinions were known, there were arguments, different positions, and now with the conflict in the making, the same voice is always heard. It remains to be seen whether Russia accepts the condition that is being imposed on it because its response could change the course of history. This analysis is part of the 2366th issue of the printed edition of Proceso, published on March 6, 2022, whose digital edition can be purchased at this link.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220309ei38000ur\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
