\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Despite covid-19 pandemic, \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2  said that Mexico is in a good fiscal position\b0\par\par\uc2 700 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juni 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 On June 9, President \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  announced a new change in his cabinet. \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2 , who had headed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Public Credit (SHCP)\uc2 , will be proposed as governor of the \uc2 Bank of Mexico (Banxico)\uc2 . Instead, Rogelio Ramirez de la O will be in charge of running the country's finances.\par \par \uc2 Thus, a month after leaving his office in the National Palace, the official received journalist Hernan Gomez to talk about his management at the head of the agency. He explained that his \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's public finances was interrupted by the COVID-19 pandemic, a situation that afflicts everyone.\par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, Herrera Gutierrez said that the federal administration has been able to overcome the adverse conditions generated by the disease, because in addition to the fact that the transmission of the SARS-CoV-2 virus has decreased, the secretary stressed that the country's fiscal position is favorable.\par \par \uc2 "What is going through a difficult time is the world, because of the pandemic and because of the economic impact on the pandemic. But it seems to me that in these complex conditions, we managed to get this out of the way. We have the pandemic today at very low levels, with relatively lower levels of contagion, and the fiscal position is coming out much better."\par \par \uc2 According to his explanation, there are countries that bet on debt trying to overcome the crisis soon, however, today they are involved in serious fiscal problems.\par \par \uc2 As for his candidacy to head \uc2 Banxico\uc2 , the official said he feels very flattered, since for an economist, "being in the Treasury or being in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is like for a footballer to play for Barcelona or Real Madrid."\par \par \uc2 As a balance, he recalled that one of the main challenges he faced at the head of the SHCP was the task of making sure that there were sufficient resources to combat the presence of the virus and, in addition, to maintain stable public finances.\par \par \uc2 "You don't choose the circumstances, but what you have to be is to know how to face them, so the most important thing is to make sure that we could contribute to keeping the country afloat in an extraordinarily painful process. We had to make sure that there were resources for the hospitals, for the vaccines and that we could keep the public finances stable."\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, he made it clear that his working relationship with President \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  has worked on the best terms. "The president listens, but requires and demands arguments, it is not giving a blank check," he said. In addition to this, he defended that he has the necessary experience to assume the position for which the president has nominated him.\par \par \uc2 Surrounded by buildings of historical, political and cultural value, the office of the secretary of finance is located facing the Zocalo in Mexico City. Before taking the nineteenth-century elevator to get to his cubicle, \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2  recounted what a morning is like for someone who occupies his position.\par \par \uc2 The first thing it monitors upon awakening are the economic variables that affect the country. According to the secretary, these are the price of oil and the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate in general has been fine except just as the pandemic started. The pandemic brought an exacerbation to investors' risk because no one knew what was going to happen, how long it was going to last, and what they did is: they pulled their investments from emerging countries, including Mexico, into hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , particularly the dollar. Then, in February of last year, the Mexican peso went from 18 pesos per dollar to 25.3 pesos per dollar in just five weeks," said the graduate of the Universidad Aut\u243\'00\'F3noma Metropolitana (UAM).\par \par \uc2 CONTINUE READING:\par \par \uc2 Who is \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2  and how a betrayal in AMLO's cabinet boosted his career\par \par \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2  will be proposed as governor of the Bank of Mexico; Rogelio Ram\u237\'00\'EDrez de la O. will replace him in the Treasury\par \par \uc2 Who is Rogelio Ram\u237\'00\'EDrez de la O: the new head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210616eh6g002kt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
