\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 What do the markets expect for this Wednesday, May 12th?\b0\par\par\uc2 483 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Mai 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 By the middle of the week, participants' attention will be in figures for inflation, energy inventories and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by members of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the agenda will have data available from INEGI and the Ministry of Labour. Meanwhile, mortgage, energy inventories and inflation data are expected in the United States, and in Europe the agenda will be dominated by data on price advances.\par \par \uc2 Mexico\par \par \uc2 The information will begin at about 6:00 a.m. when INEGI publishes indicators of industrial activity during March.\par \par \uc2 In addition, the Secretariat of Labour and Social Security (STPS) is expected to reveal figures for formal job creation during April.\par \par \uc2 United States\par \par \uc2 Information will be available from 6:00 a.m., with data from the \uc2 Mortgage Bankers Association\uc2  that will disclose the number of mortgage applications as of May 7. The last reported data, a week earlier, revealed that requests increased by 0.9 percent.\par \par \uc2 Later, at 7:30 a.m., the Bureau of Labour Statistics will publish inflation indicators during April; analysts estimate that the price increase is around an annualized rate of 3.6 percent, above 2.6 percent earlier and above the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target. At a monthly rate, forecasts estimate that inflation is around 0.2 percent.\par \par \uc2 At 8:00 a.m., \uc2 Richard Clarida\uc2 , Vice President of the Fed, will give a speech on the economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 At 8:05 a.m., \uc2 Eric Rosengren\uc2 , president of the Boston Fed, will speak to Harvard Law School about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's outlook and digital \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Later, at 9:30 a.m., the \uc2 Energy Information Administration\uc2  (EIA) will release oil inventories and their derivatives as of May 7.\par \par \uc2 An hour later, at 10:30 a.m., the Treasury Department will reopen a short-term bond auction (T-Bills) for $35 billion liquidity management in a 119-day \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; another 41 billion will be auctioned at noon, but this time it will be 10-year Treasury Notes.\par \par \uc2 At noon, \uc2 Raphael Bostic\uc2 , president of the Atlanta Fed, will speak at a webinar.\par \par \uc2 At 12:30 a.m., \uc2 Patrick Harker\uc2 , president of the Philadelphia Fed, will participate in an event to discuss higher education.\par \par \uc2 At 1:00 a.m., the Treasury Department will have monthly budget data during April.\par \par \uc2 Europe\par \par \uc2 The information to be followed will be data on business investment, trade balance and industrial production in the United Kingdom in March, and in that country will also highlight the GDP data in the first quarter of the year.\par \par \uc2 For the Eurozone, there will be data on industrial production in the third month of the year, where a 1% vs. February progress and 11.5% annual growth are expected.\par \par \uc2 Inflation figures will be revealed in Germany and France during April; there will also be \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by economic authorities in the Eurozone.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210512eh5c003nw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
