\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 US launches "first warning" to Mexico over peso price against dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 881 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 April 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's government fears that fiscal austerity and hostile investment climate in Mexico will impede an adjustment in the trade balance with the country, which has a negative balance for the US.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's growing trade surplus with the United States has already aroused the strangeness of Treasury Department officials, as \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's entity decided to give a "first warning" to the neighboring country with the start of monitoring of trades by pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The criteria for the US to have decided to include \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its "close monitoring" list are alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, current account surplus of at least 2% of GDP and/or a bulging trade surplus.\par \par \uc2 Mexico closed 2020 with a trade surplus with its main partner at nearly $112.722 billion (mdd). A trend that continued during January and February of this year, with a cumulative of about 15,940 mdd, indicate data from the \uc2 US government\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For Alfredo Couti\u241\'00\'F1o, director for Latin America at Moody's Analytics, while acknowledging the existence of a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for free floating and minimal \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by mexican authorities, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's government is "concerned" about policies implemented by the Mexican government that have an indirect effect on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  parity and current account surplus\par \par \uc2 "Specificly, the northern neighbor's authority is concerned about the persistent policy of fiscal austerity and the hostile climate for private investment that together hold domestic demand depressed, thereby promoting a persistent trade and current account surplus, hampering an automatic rebalancing of Mexican external accounts to the detriment of Americans" , he commented in an interview via email.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico has had a trade surplus of more than 20,000 mdd with the United States since 1999 and by 2020 the current account surplus averaged 2.4% (relative to GDP). This would lead to Mexico being included in the list, but not for the first time, because the trade and current account criteria are not the first time Mexico has reached them," Gabriela Siller, Director of Financial Economic Analysis at Banco Base, said.\par \par \uc2 However, Felipe Hernandez, \uc2 Economist\uc2  for Latin America at Bloomberg Economics, considered the possibility that the United States sanctions Mexico is much lower in a Biden administration than under the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 "The trade relationship is very important and I don't see sanctions in this administration," the expert said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  ensures that this surveillance will be transitional and that the bilateral balance will be adjusted to pre-pandemic levels as the economic recovery occurs.\par \par \uc2 "Once we look at the effects associated with this set of policies and be clear how many are related to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is when it will be possible to determine whether Mexico actually falls into a category of country that manipulates the exchange rate or not and I think in that sense it is very rare for it to act in that regard," said V\u237\'00\'EDctor G\u243\'00\'F3mez , deputy director of economic analysis of Finamex Casa de Bolsa.\par \par \uc2 For Moody's economist, the signal sent about Mexico is not positive and adds to the negative factors that can cloud the country's economic future as the US is particularly concerned about fiscal management.\par \par \uc2 The Treasury's report also advanced that with AMLO's government policies, U.S. renewable energy exports to Mexico are expected to shrink, and this in turn will mean a bilateral trade surplus for Mexico.\par \par \uc2 "Mexico's economic policies jeopardize the trade relationship with the United States. Not for trying to generate more growth for Mexico (which would be a positive thing), but for changing the rules of the game and affecting the interests of other countries," Siller said.\par \par \uc2 Janneth Quiroz, deputy director of analysis at Monex Casa de Bolsa, said that considering that the United States is Mexico's largest trading partner with more than 80% of exports, it is the country that will be most interested in Mexico practicing a regulation that is established internationally.\par \par \uc2 For Quiroz, the US announcement is a call to the Mexican authorities to remember that Mexico is not isolated from the rest of the countries and is part of an international community.\par \par \uc2 "It has signed trade agreements that must comply with and comply with these pacts must be a priority for economic authorities in the country," she said.\par \par \uc2 Quiroz considered that respecting trade agreements will give investor guarantees and improve the investment climate in the country.\par \par \uc2 "The United States somehow raised its voice to say 'we are watching over the economic policy that our trading partners also implement' and it is certainly important for Mexico to comply with these regulations and it is certainly news to ensure and try to ensure that Mexico does not deviate from all these reforms of the policies that have been implemented" Said.\par \par \uc2 The peso closed Tuesday's session with a depreciation of 0.62% or 12.2 cents, to be quoted at 19.94 units per dollar, due to good economic data and US business performance and despite an environment of worsening the coronavirus pandemic globally.\par \par \uc2 The US entry launches a "first warning" to Mexico for the price of the peso against the dollar appears first in I-Xport.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210422eh4l0018r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
