\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Why a "treasure" from porfirio D\u237\'00\'EDaz's era could turn Mexico into a world power\b0\par\par\uc2 1,083 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A "treasure" of more than 830 billion pesos could make Mexico a world power, assured Infobae M\u233\'00\'E9xico Rogelio Amparan, a member of the Joint Private Fund for Autonomous Heritage.\par \par \uc2 We're going to check it out, because if this is real. or we have it, Mexico is really going to become a power, because to do everything you want, you need resources\par \par \uc2 Since the country achieved its independence from the Spanish Crown, in 1821, a series of "out-of-book" deposits have been generated to compensate the legitimate owners of the Mexican territory, the original communities, for the extraction of natural wealth at the hands of nations of great economic importance.\par \par \uc2 "So, what is a fact, because we came to know all these deposits at some point, when we do a compliance with England, they throw away all the information and it is amazing, was the confirmation a few years ago that there were so many gold deposits of different denominations and weight, that the Mexican state made to concentrate them and, at the time , to compensate the entire Mexican population through the administration of their \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Amparan told Infobae Mexico.\par \par \uc2 However, it was until Porfiriato, a thirty-year period in which General Porfirio D\u237\'00\'EDaz was president of Mexico, that such contributions became more relevant.\par \par \uc2 This moment in history is characterized by political, social and economic stability, as it opened the door to important foreign investors who managed to accelerate commercial activity. Mexico's Gross Domestic Product from 1877 to 1910 was impressive for its time; real GDP per capita remained at levels of 2.1% per year.\par \par \uc2 Compared to other more developed countries, according to economist Timothy J. Kehoe, "[...] Porphyriato was the period - except for the 1950-1981 import substitution period - in which Mexico is comparable to the United States."\par \par \uc2 Already with Plutarco El\u237\'00\'EDas Calles at the head of the Federal Executive, a decree is issued to begin with the compensation of indigenous peoples in the future, an amount that was formed by the accumulated deposits and an appraisal of Mexican lands.\par \par \uc2 "The deposits themselves form something called the Single Support Capital Account (CUCA) from which the entire population becomes an active partner, three generations of 33 years have passed and Mexico has the right to collect it up to the fourth generation, but Mexico should be receiving dividends from that unique contribution account to distribute them to its entire population," explained Mauricio Montijo spokesman Lucero , single administrator and liquidator agent of the FMPPA.\par \par \uc2 Montijo Lucero acquired the right to manage the fund for the appointment given to his family, when El\u237\'00\'EDas Calles, in 1928, began the registration process from the updating of particular committees of all the indigenous communities of the country.\par \par \uc2 "It was Grandma, Dad and then Mauritius who has been following up. This right was granted to it when those 33 years expire, after those deposits in that third period Mexico can now automatically access through its common representative the yields generated by that account and those huge yields, Mauritius talks about 822 million initially, but right now we go in eight hundred and thirty-somethings," he said.\par \par \uc2 It has been proven that everything Mauritius says is real, that \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a great treasure\par \par \uc2 It would take the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Mexican State, with the support of a diplomatic corps, for the Joint Private Fund of Autonomous Heritage to initiate a process of repatriation of resources. For this reason, the members of that body took with optimism theinitiative of \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  on indegar about the "treasure".\par \par \uc2 At a morning press conference on January 19, the Mexican representative reported that \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2 , Secretary of Finance and Public Credit, was given the instruction to investigate the fortune he would be abroad.\par \par \uc2 "We have heard this version on other occasions, but we have no evidence, there is no evidence that this is real, of course we do not close any files that have to do with these facts, with the possibility that there is money abroad that is from Mexico, that does not prescribe; if investigated, if you have elements, if tested, if it is real; then the government would act to demand the return of that wealth for the benefit of the people of Mexico, but there is now no information on that," he said on January 19.\par \par \uc2 With these resources, rogelio Amparan said, Mexico gained financial independence. In addition, an investment in four main axes could be generated among the country's 2,458 municipalities: education, health, economic development and food.\par \par \uc2 "If we give that money to each inhabitant, because we are going to collapse the country and that is not the idea, it is a smart financial action that should apply that investment and make the whole population work for their communities, under that case let's say hypothetical the amount towards each inhabitant generates a source of investment because the stock market does not withdraw , it is maintained and what it produces is what is being withdrawn and is being invested in the four areas of sustainable development," he said.\par \par \uc2 However, this information has not been disclosed to the population. According to the FMPPA member, there are political and business domes that Mexico does not want to regain its value in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, investment development. "[...] that part is the one that the public administration doesn't like very much because it thinks we're trying to generate an alternate government and it's not."\par \par \uc2 "Our intention is not to be in confrontation with anyone, let alone the president of the republic, the intention is to give him the most powerful tool that the president of the republic can access, to access the whole plan he brings to develop this country and is genuine," he added.\par \par \uc2 READ ON:\par \par \uc2 Neither Santa Anna sold half of Mexico nor the Malinche was a traitor: five myths in history\par \par \uc2 From Santa Anna to Porfirio D\u237\'00\'EDaz: who is among the great "villains" of Mexico's history\par \par \uc2 AMLO ordered the investigation of the whereabouts of an 822 billion "treasure" abroad dating back to the time of Porfirio D\u237\'00\'EDaz\par \par \uc2 Do you have a treasure in your wallet: these are the Mexican coins and banknotes that are worth a fortune\par \par \uc2 Revolution money worth gold: old coins and banknotes are traded in thousands of pesos\par \par \uc2 The true heritage that Porfirio D\u237\'00\'EDaz left to Mexicans\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210306eh3600193\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
