\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Interventionist \highlight\uc2  policies in pandemic could exacerbate credit risk: \uc2 Fitch Ratings\b0\par\par\uc2 503 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY (apro).- Qualifying agency \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  warned that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies amid the pandemic could exacerbate credit risk for financial institutions in Mexico and Latin America.\par \par \uc2 According to the firm, the increased risk of government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  arising from legislation may expose banks to international sanctions.\par \par \uc2 "Mexican lawmakers delayed the debate on a controversial bill recently passed by its Senate of the Republic, which requires the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 Banxico\uc2 ) to buy excess foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in cash until February 2021," notes the report entitled "Non-Orthodox policies in Latam would stress financial institutions in the midst of the crisis."\par \par \uc2 Fitch warned that while this bill is intended to benefit people receiving remittances or cash dollars from tourist activity, this exposes \uc2 Banxico\uc2  to the risk of buying U.S. dollars from illegal or un traceable sources. In the meantime, major banks support efforts to combat the proposal.\par \par \uc2 According to the rating agency, the implementation of these initiatives is currently at very early stages, either in simple initiative or bill, in countries such as Mexico, Panama and Peru.\par \par \uc2 However, Costa Rica has had interest rate limits since July 2020 and Fitch expects that to negatively influence the financial and credit profiles of private banks.\par \par \uc2 The effects on Honduras, Guatemala, El Salvador, Bolivia and Argentina are varied and some have experienced slowdowns in loan growth, deteriorating credit quality or pressure on margins, as a result of interest rate caps and government tariff restrictions.\par \par \uc2 According to the analysis, these policies are unlikely to push the credit ratings of large banks in the short term, as they benefit from the scale and diversification of their portfolios.\par \par \uc2 However, he clarified, they could extend the time required for small and medium-sized banks and non-bank financial institutions (IFNBs) in specialized sectors to recover from the economic consequences of the pandemic.\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2 , unrthodox and populist policies, such as limiting interest rates on products -- such as consumer or microfinance loans--, reducing commissions, requiring loan deadlines, and implementing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation, have been discussed with Latin American authorities since before the pandemic crisis.\par \par \uc2 However, the authorities have increasingly used these policies to support debtors and promote credit expansion to respond to the region's severe economic downturn.\par \par \uc2 Compulsory loans to sectors could result in greater risks to banks. They could also involve a reduction in IFNB's appetite to extend credit to risky segments.\par \par \uc2 The report highlights that larger and more diversified banks should be able to offset the margin pressure of interest rate caps through cost-cutting measures and the use of alternative channels, such as digital and online, for the origination and collection of credits.\par \par \uc2 However, small and medium-sized banks and IFNBs in specialized sectors such as microcredit or consumer loans will be more affected by higher operating, lending and funding costs.\par \par \uc2 "Commissions and fees could help mitigate the impact of margins, but commission collection is being restricted with proposed reductions insome Latin American countries," Fitch added.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210129eh1s001ha\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
