\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The reform that the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  does need\b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Dezember 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Central banks in the world can have one or two of these main objectives; the first is to maintain the purchasing power of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that is, to avoid inflation and the second is to avoid unemployment.\par \par \uc2 The two phenomena of both inflation and unemployment are regarded as the greatest enemies for society economically. Inflation, the widespread increase in prices, extracts, erodes, eliminates the purchasing power of money and has regressive effects because it affects the most humble people they least have. On the other hand, unemployment is also a major enemy for the economy for obvious reasons.\par \par \uc2 Central banks are the bodies responsible for exercising a country's monetary policy and can deal with these two terrible phenomena; inflation and unemployment. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implements an expansive monetary policy by increasing the monetary supply in the economy, it can thereby promote the activation of the economy, which will ultimately result in job creation, and in the same way to avoid an inflationary process it can contract the money supply to achieve it.\par \par \uc2 The point is that in our country the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  has only one mandate that is to maintain the purchasing power of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but it does not have the mandate to avoid unemployment, which must be corrected as soon as possible by allowing the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  with its very powerful monetary policy to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the economy to combat unemployment while always taking care to stay within an inflation target previously set by the Bank itself.\par \par \uc2 Within the central banks that enjoy this dual mandate, controlling inflation and avoiding unemployment we find the influential Federal Reserve of the United States of America, so it would not be a proposal for reckless but well-founded reform. The important thing is to put the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy to work in a dual mandate, to avoid inflation and also unemployment, which would be very much in line with the current administration focused on improving the well-being of citizens, especially the most unfortunate.\par \par \uc2 Mtro. Jes\u250\'00\'FAs Torres G\u243\'00\'F3mez\par \par \uc2 Professor at the International School of Law and Jurisprudence.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201220egck0028q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
