\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The elephant in the living room: the dollars!\b0\par\par\uc2 678 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Dezember 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Santiago Nieto, owner of the UIF, says that the 2019-2020 National Risk Assessment on money laundering in Mexico detects the flow of dollars in cash as a vulnerability, but that it is "not high".\par \par \uc2 And yes, it's not high, but it exists! The volume of dollars repatriated is approximately 7 billion and of these, 4 thousand are exported through \uc2 Bank of America\uc2 , including those of Citibanamex, because in the business of correspondents in the United States, of 90 participants, there are 3 "taking the risk" that the \uc2 FDIC\uc2  or the OCC will say that their money laundering screening procedures are insufficient and must end , if you are sorry to lose your bank license and have to take on million-dollar fines.\par \par \uc2 In the last 13 years, the problem of de-risking and de-banking has been discussed in different forums. Result: committees and commitments and no solution.\par \par \uc2 In the ABM it has always been present in the agenda of young banks. Our esteemed Luis Robles (may he rest in peace), being vice president of the Association, came to hire Promontory to establish a "compliance certification" process, because much GAFI and FSB, but there is no clear criterion defined between the financial authorities of Mexico and the United States so that a bank cannot enter into contracts for the exclusion of "risk", even though in its country of origin it is certified by the supervisor and the regulator (in this case the CNBV or the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 ) to comply with money laundering rules.\par \par \uc2 It has been mentioned that it is a problem of a single bank: Azteca. And no, he's not the only one, and it's also not true that he took his dollars and couldn't export them because the \uc2 FDIC\uc2  ordered a cease-and-desist procedure to CBW Bank in Weir, Kansas, last September.\par \par \uc2 This bank had a CD, but not azteca, but its exit left only two banks in international correspondent. Imagine the commission! for taking dollars.\par \par \uc2 However, the proposed reform has created a complicated situation and for some it sets a serious precedent.\par \par \uc2 Last night and faced with the possibility that the initiative to reform section 20 of the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  Act for the central institute to buy the surplus dollars of Mexican banks, \uc2 Moody's\uc2 , the sovereign debt qualifier that keeps the country's credit at the highest investment grade, notes that the adoption of the reform to the law would have a "negative" material effect , that is, the ideal pretext to lower the rating.\par \par \uc2 Why the widespread reaction of the financial community? It is not de-risking, nor the adverse effects it has on the population sending and receiving remittances in cash, but that a majority in Congress, such as the one that is disciplined today, could be able to reform the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's law to ask them to buy all of \uc2 Pemex\uc2 's debt. It's the precedent that scares and a lot.\par \par \uc2 For the time being, D\u237\'00\'EDaz de Le\u243\'00\'F3n proposed a solution to get the elephant out of the room: to make Mexico's money laundering oversight model credible.\par \par \uc2 Build a technology platform that allows a better understanding of these risks. Cash \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transaction information would be centralized so that banks can know statistical data on the transactions their clients perform with other entities in the financial sector so that they can make a deeper and more complete diligence (money laundering) process.\par \par \uc2 U.S. banks may consult this platform to complete the customer knowledge process using the information they receive. With this, Mexican banks would be in a position to demonstrate to their counterparts that they serve as correspondent banks that their customer knowledge and due diligence processes are robust enoughto maintain international correspondentry.\par \par \uc2 Cash dollars could be repatriated to the United States at lower cost and greater efficiency, without the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as proposed in the draft decree. Just put it in writing and with dates to be fulfilled!\par \par \par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201215egcf002nl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
