\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Banxico\uc2  is exposed with meaningless law\b0\par\par\uc2 554 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Dezember 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 With changes to the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  Act passed Wednesday by the Senate, the goal of achieving a better exchange price for users will not be achieved, but international reserves are put at risk.\par \par \uc2 The initiative, which was taken over by Deputies, aims to force \uc2 Banxico\uc2  to buy the cash \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that financial institutions fail to repatriate through their correspondents abroad and it would be the same institutions that define how much they did not repatriate and should buy from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The flow begins with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - mostly dollars - that arrive in cash in the country and are exchanged in financial institutions, which subsequently seek to sell them either to people in the country who require those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  or abroad.\par \par \uc2 The main argument for changes to the Act points out that by not being able to repatriate all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , institutions face higher costs than moving to the exchange rates they offer.\par \par \uc2 However, in a technical note sent to the Senate, \uc2 Banxico\uc2  clarified that financial institutions have mechanisms to repatriate through correspondents, and a total of $4.732 billion raised in cash between January and September, only 2% have not been repatriated and is kept in bank vaults.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has rejected the reform and warned that by buying the dollars in cash it takes the risk that these resources will be of illicit origin, which it would have to integrate into its reserves, as would be required by the new Law.\par \par \uc2 It detailed that 99% of remittances reach the country through wire transfers, so the measure would be aiming to serve only that remaining 1%.\par \par \uc2 "This risk would not only be limited to the amounts of cash \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  captured by the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  in accordance with the above, but could extend to the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  of international reserves in the possession of the Institute," he said.\par \par \uc2 Gabriela Siller, Director of Economic and Financial Analysis at Banco Base, explained that by forcing \uc2 Banxico\uc2  to buy dollars that credit institutions cannot place, she is exposed to being subject to penalties for resources of possible illicit origin.\par \par \uc2 And with this, the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  (Fed) or any other \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could freeze \uc2 Banxico\uc2 's accounts and assets, including international reserves.\par \par \uc2 "International reserves support the circulator, that is, Mexico's cash," he said.\par \par \uc2 "Thus, in the event of a freeze on reserves, there would no longer be an endorsement of the money, leading to a balance-of-payments crisis and a depreciation of the peso."\par \par \uc2 Risk of infection\par \par \uc2 The initiative already approved by Senators would expose \uc2 Banxico\uc2  to pollute his reserves with dirty money.\par \par \uc2 (Current acquisition and destination of cash \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and how \uc2 Banxico\uc2  would be affected with the initiative)\par \par \uc2 Currently\par \par \uc2 Commercial banks\par \par \uc2 Capture\par \par \uc2 (buy with security filters)\par \par \uc2 Sell\par \par \uc2 They have too much left, with a potentially dirty part\par \par \uc2 Solid banks change them with others abroad\par \par \uc2 Only a small part is kept in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 BANXICO DOES NOT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 GOING FORWARD?\par \par \uc2 It would increase the collection of dollars in cash in banks\par \par \uc2 They would force \uc2 Banxico\uc2  to buy possible dirty money\par \par \uc2 Their reserves would be polluted\par \par \uc2 Implications\par \par \uc2 - Freezing \uc2 Banxico\uc2  accounts and assets\par \par \uc2 - It would be prevented from conducting international transactions\par \par \uc2 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation\par \par \uc2 - Loss of purchasing value\par \par \uc2 - Increased perception of risk in Mexico\par \par \uc2 - Damage to the entire Mexican financial system\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201211egcb0054i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
