\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Mexico weathered the storm over the peso and increased its reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 496 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 When the Mexican peso fell to historic lows earlier this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  remained on the sidelines, saving ammunition. It's a policy that may be starting to pay off.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  refrained from using its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves even when the peso led down to emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in late March. This action was very contrasting with that of its peers in developing countries.\par \par \uc2 The bank seems to have weathered the storm. After losing 25% of its value until March 23, the peso stabilized, even as oil prices fell and the coronavirus pandemic threatened to cut off to 12% of gross domestic product. By comparison, Brazil\u8212\'20\'14which has spent $48 billion on spot market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14has seen a 27% depreciation of its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, while the president, Jair Bolsonaro, usded a political storm.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 Banxico\uc2  continues to choose to use its swap program for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  management," said Ilya Gofshteyn, a Strata at \uc2 Standard Chartered\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 The policy has left Mexico in an almost unique position among emerging markets, as it registers an increase in its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves this year. Reserves reached $186.1 billion in May, the highest since August 2015.\par \par \uc2 The country has the lowest share of gross reserves on average annual imports among major Latin American peers.To provide liquidity to the market, \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  used a \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  swap line of $60 billion twice in April and sold a total of $10 billion in the market in the form of dollar credit. The country also supplies non-deliverable forwards settled in pesos, a measure similar to Brazil and Chile.\par \par \uc2 The peso "remains the preferred emerging market indicator among investors and \uc2 Banxico\uc2  will hesitate to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly through selling," Gofshteyn said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have had few options. The country has the lowest share of gross reserves on average annual imports among major Latin American peers. In relation to its reserves, Mexico's potential financing needs in the event of a major external shock will be high, according to Marcelo Carvalho and Luiz Peixoto, emerging market analysts at London-based \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . South Africa, Egypt, Chile, Colombia and Turkey are also among the vulnerable nations.\par \par \uc2 After simulating a global crisis in exports, tourism, remittances, foreign direct investment and emerging market portfolio flows, Carvalho and Peixoto found that the impact on the balance of payments could reach 6.9% of Mexico's GDP and 4.7% of Brazil's GDP. Assuming a 90% renewal of short-term external debt, total external financing needs would reach about 5.1% in Brazil and 7.5% for Mexico.\par \par \uc2 MORE ABOUT OTHER TOPICS:\par \par \uc2 Mexican peso down falling from weak US employment data\par \par \uc2 These are states where violence causes up to 14 times more deaths than coronavirus\par \par \uc2 By coronavirus, Tianguis Tur\u237\'00\'EDstico in Merida was postponed until 2021; there will be an editiondigital in September of this year\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200506eg56005i7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex