\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  to speak to \uc2 Banxico\uc2  about remnants of foreign reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Mexican President \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  will meet with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  about unexpected remnants of the bank's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves after the peso crash this year.\par \par \uc2 At a morning press conference, the president said he would talk to the bank's board members about the remnant, raising speculation that he will now request a payment of this year's earnings, even though they would normally be paid in April 2021.\par \par \uc2 The problem for the president is that there is no remnant in 2019 as the weight was regained that year. Given the 27% drop in weight this year and the current level of reserves, Benito Berber, chief economist for Latin America at \uc2 Natixis North America\uc2 , estimates that around 866 billion pesos (US$36 billion) could be paid to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This would represent a significant entry for a government suffering from liquidity problems.\par \par \uc2 "It would be very controversial if they made some kind of breakthrough," Berber said. "It would be very close to government financing by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But given the shock, the market might not take it negatively, especially if the funds are used to support the economy."\par \par \uc2 Banxico\uc2  has the final say on how much is actually sent, and the money goes to debt reduction (Photo: REUTERS/Daniel Becerril) (DANIEL BECERRIL/)A presidential spokesman said the meeting will take place Thursday after AMLO initially said it would be today.\par \par \uc2 Banxico\uc2  has the final say on how much is actually sent, and the money goes to debt reduction. The bank may refuse to send a prepayment as the final figures for weight depreciation and reserves are not included.\par \par \uc2 "They don't have to transfer everything," said Eduardo Suarez, Scotiabank's strata in Mexico City. "You can't, partly because at this time you don't know how much it will be."\par \par \uc2 However, for \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2 , who has made fiscal strength a priority even in the midst of the coronavirus crisis, additional \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  funds will be attractive.\par \par \uc2 "This surplus will help us avoid debt growth," he told reporters during the conference.\par \par \uc2 MORE ON THIS TOPIC:\par \par \uc2 Coronavirus in Mexico: in which states there is the greatest risk of contagion\par \par \uc2 Five states reserve certain covid-19 sick data: they argue it's to avoid panic and discrimination\par \par \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  reiterated his thanks to Trump for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in "tense" negotiation with OPEC: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  was the exception"\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200415eg4f0044w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
