\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Strengthens \uc2 Banxico\uc2  international reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 407 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 If the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  were to make direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from international reserves, it would have $185.509 million at its disposal.\par \par \uc2 This, incorporating the $1.334 million increase that was completed in the week of March 20-27.\par \par \uc2 This weekly increase in the international reserve is the result of a change in the valuation of international assets of $884 million and $450 million sold by \uc2 Pemex\uc2  to the central institute.\par \par \uc2 Asset valuation is the movement resulting from the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with respect to the various \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that make up the international reserve.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar acquis, i.e. international reserves, completed an accumulation of $4.631 million. This is the fastest rate of accumulation for a similar period since 2015, only beyond the history reached in 2014, when reserves were strengthened by $6.163 million in the same period.\par \par \uc2 In the 13 weeks of the year, the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  has recorded eight weekly accumulations of reserves totaling $5.965 million. However, this increase in reserves has been affected by the cumulative reductions in four weeks, which totalled $1.634 million.\par \par \uc2 In this year, \uc2 Pemex\uc2  has contributed 1.733 million of this provision of dollars, as by law it must exchange the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  resulting from its oil sales in the \uc2 Banxico\uc2 . Since the fall in hydrocarbon production began in 2015, targeted reserve accumulation has been limited.\par \par \uc2 IMF\uc2  strengthens dollar acquisSince 2009, Mexico has had an open credit line at the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , which guarantees access to a certain amount of dollars, currently $61 billion, if required by the \uc2 Banxico\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 This \uc2 IMF\uc2  facility for Mexico guarantees the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  the possibility of putting together a strategy in the event of a high volatility episode, as it could complement international reserves with this FCL.\par \par \uc2 So by adding up to the $185.509 million that are part of the international reserves, with the $61 billion open line at the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  can count on liquidity in dollars of up to $246.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Notwithstanding \uc2 Banxico\uc2 's arsenal of dollars that represents access to this Flexible Credit Line, its use comes at a cost, because even if they are resources that would be available they would have to be documented as public debt. Mexico has ceased to be an \uc2 IMF\uc2  debtor since 2000.\par \par \uc2 [email protected]\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200401eg41000vt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
