\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 4 \uc2 Banxico\uc2  measures to guarantee liquidity for banks\b0\par\par\uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico (Banxico)\uc2 released four measures that seek to guarantee liquidity for banks and corporate companies that may even require U.S. dollars in the face of deteriorating global financial conditions, because of the contingency caused by the spread of Covid-19 coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Measures involving the use of the $60 billion that \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  will exchange with the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 (Fed)on the swap line announced Thursday, March 19.\par \par \uc2 The first action is to reduce the Monetary Regulation Deposit (DRM) held by the multiple banking and development institutions at the Central Institute, amounting to 50 billion pesos.\par \par \uc2 The objective of this measure is to improve the liquidity and ability to provide loans from banks, as well as to maintain or expand lines of credit. Currently the total amount of the DRM is 320 billion pesos, and the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  will sterilize the monetary impact of this measure that will take place on April 1 of this year.\par \par \uc2 The second action is also aimed at multiple banking and involves the cut in the cost of loans or reports between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and financial institutions, which currently fluctuates between 2 and 2.2 times the objective of \uc2 Banxico\uc2 'sone-day interbank interest rate. The measure is to halve this cost and place it at 1.1 times the rate target. This measure is called Ordinary Additional Liquidity Facility; is available since 2008 and the change will take effect from April 1.\par \par \uc2 The third measure announced by \uc2 Banxico\uc2  is aimed at guaranteeing liquidity in dollars,and was taken by instruction from the Exchange Commission where the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  also participates. This facility will be financed by the temporary \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  mechanism, known as the swap line,established with the Fed in the amount of $60 billion.\par \par \uc2 And the fourth action is a collaboration with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen the Government Debt Market Trainers Program that will also come into force on April 1.\par \par \uc2 Discouraging speculationIf the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to resort to direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market, it would have $245.619 million available that it could use to try to order the sharp weight movements against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 This amount comes from adding up international reserves, amounting to $184,619 million as of March 13 and $61 billion available on mexico's Flexible Credit Line at the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 If these resources were not sufficient, thanks to the open swap line with the Fed,\uc2 Banco de Mexico\uc2  would have another $60 billion available.\par \par \uc2 According to the Founder and Coordinator of UNAM's Center for Model modeling and Economic Forecasting (CEMPE), Eduardo Loria, the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  by incorporating in the package, the auctions of dollars from the resources of the swap line with the Fed , the signal is being sent that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dollars to prevent the exchange rate from moving to the market's liking.\par \par \uc2 "It is to give a message that we have sufficient liquidity to prevent it from happening to us as 1982, 1985 and 1994. The intention is to discourage speculative attitudes against the exchange rate, because if they demand dollars and want to take them out, the BankMexico has how to offer more to arm in quotation marks and avoid larger depreciations."Message receivedBNP Parib\u225\'00\'E1s strategists and the consultancy Pantheon Macroeconomics, admit that the additional measures announced by \uc2 Banco de Mexico\uc2  to strengthen liquidity measures as much as possible, send the signal of a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with robust resources.\par \par \uc2 On the decision to use the swap line to auction dollars between credit institutions, BNP Parib\u225\'00\'E1s' chief economist for Mexico and Colombia, Joel Virgen, says it is optimal to secure liquidity even in dollars.\par \par \uc2 He adds that leaving international reserves intact and keeping the Flexible Credit Line open, the message is sent that they have a large and robust wealth of dollar resources that they can use in case the market warrants it.\par \par \uc2 From London, the senior economist for Latin America at Pantheon Macroeconomics, Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Abbey, believes that these measures aim to promote and improve the functioning of domestic financial markets.\par \par \uc2 However, it underlines what the Governing Board itself said in the communiqu\u233\'00\'E9, in order to assert that "perseverance in strengthening macroeconomic fundamentals and in the adoption of the necessary actions in both fiscal and fiscal policies and to contribute to a successful adjustment of domestic financial markets and the economy in general."\par \par \uc2 Both strategists agree that global volatility will persist and as the next \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  meeting is scheduled until May, there is a wide possibility that an additional off-calendar cut will be resubmitted.\par \par \uc2 [email protected]\par \par \uc2 Kg\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200322eg3m002ch\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
