\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Mexico's international reserves recorded its biggest drop in three years due to investment losses\b0\par\par\uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Mexico's international reserves fell last week by $952 million, mainly due to the change in the valuation of the assets that make up them, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The fall of the indicator is the largest since January 2017, when Donald Trump's U.S. presidential election took the peso to a historic low and triggered several bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 Banxico\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The weekly reduction in the international reserve of $952 million was mainly the result of a change in the valuation of the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 's international assets," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported.\par \par \uc2 Banxico\uc2  Governor Alejandro D\u237\'00\'EDaz de Le\u243\'00\'F3n said last week that a direct sale of dollars to the exchange market in the current context is among the tools the institution has, but that the preference is to use exchange rate hedges.\par \par \uc2 2019 could be the worst year of the decade for the Mexican economy (Photo: Pxhere)The Mexican peso depreciated on Wednesday by twelfth consecutive session to a new historic low, above 24 units per dollar, due to persistent fears about the economic impact of the coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Due to the depreciation, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced measures such as a swap of government debt instruments, as well as auctions of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges.\par \par \uc2 Peso falls to new all-time low, oversulsing 24-dollar barrier\par \par \uc2 In the current six-year age, the Mexican peso has devalued 49% against the US dollar.The Mexican peso depreciated on Wednesday by twelfth consecutive session to a new historic low, due to persistent fears of the economic impact of the coronavirus and a sharp decline in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading at 23.81 per dollar, with a 3.81% depreciation versus 22.9367 of Tuesday's Reuters reference price. The weight fell in international \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the early morning until 24,067 units, a new all-time low.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  accumulates a retracement of more than 25% in the year.\par \par \uc2 Oil prices fell on Wednesday for the third consecutive session, with futures falling in the United States to a low of 17 years in the face of the worsening fuel demand outlook due to the suspension of travel and social life caused by the Coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 File image. A worker appears in the photograph behind the Mexican Stock Exchange logo in Mexico City. March 2, 2020. REUTERS / Gustavo Graf (GUSTAVO GRAF/)Banco Base said a lower price of crude oil raises the risk of a cut to the credit rating of Mexican state oil company \uc2 Pemex\uc2  and the country's sovereign debt. The price of the Mexican mixture could be below $18.78 per barrel on Tuesday, added in a report for itsCustomers.\par \par \uc2 Base said that during the session an exchange rate was expected to be quoted between 23.00 and 24.50 pesos per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose Wednesday to a maximum of three years against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as companies and investors concerned about the coronavirus outbreak rushed to the safe haven of the world's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sharp depreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to influence \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 's monetary policy decisions next week, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon called for a new auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges, later in the day, seeking to "promote better liquidity conditions" in the market, as well as a swap of debt instruments.\par \par \uc2 MORE ABOUT OTHER TOPICS:\par \par \uc2 Oil remains business for Mexico despite falling international prices: \uc2 L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\par \par \uc2 They detect coronavirus case after bankers' convention in Acapulco\par \par \uc2 INER workers demand a protocol that allows them to care for coronavirus sufferers\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200318eg3i0069m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
