\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Bankers, crisis and opportunity\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The themes originally planned for the 83rd Banking Convention were overtaken by the outbreak of a couple of black days in the world's financial markets.\par \par \uc2 The focus of bankers' concern, outside the work tables, was around a big question: what should the Mexican government do, not only to overcome the situation, but to emerge stronger and seize the opportunity offered by the crisis are generating the petroprice war and the expansion of the coronavirus?\par \par \uc2 Yesterday the annual convention of bankers began in the port of Acapulco, and from the night before and in the early morning the markets marked the beginning of what would later be considered as the worst day since black Monday 1987.\par \par \uc2 This Thursday, March 12, a day after President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  decided to close his borders to U.S. flights to Europe and vice versa, to prevent or contain the contagion of the Covid-19, and a couple of days after the Arabian price war began Saudi Arabia and Russia recorded a unique day of losses that affected the global financial market.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street had its worst day yesterday since Black Monday 1987. Markets in the US were painted red and in Mexico the BMV fell to its worst level since 2012.\par \par \uc2 Industrial Dow Jones fell 10%, the S&P 500 had a 9.5 percent decline. On Monday, 19 October 1987, US markets fell by more than 20%.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, a severe depreciation of the peso against the dollar was observed, which closed at 21.64 and peaked at 22.87. It could have been worse.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2  reacted and saved the weight of what may have been one of the strongest depreciations it has ever had, with hedge auctions\par \par \uc2 Mexico's Exchange Commission (integrated by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Public Credit, headed by \uc2 Arturo Herrera\uc2 , and the \uc2 Bank of Mexico\uc2 , ruled by Alejandro D\u237\'00\'EDaz de Le\u243\'00\'F3n) announced an auction of $2 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges, thereby relieved the pressure on the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Just earlier it was listed above 22 units.\par \par \uc2 And the announcement by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  of a trade in government securities of up to 40 billion pesos for others over terms longer than two years.\par \par \uc2 The announcement, especially for the coordination between the Treasury and \uc2 Banxico\uc2 , had an effect that was immediate and very positive.\par \par \uc2 Also in the morning, President \uc2 Andr\u233\'00\'E9s Manuel L\u243\'00\'F3pez Obrador\uc2  issued a message that sought to build trust by ensuring that Mexico has sound finances and growing incomes. But what was most striking was when he reiterated his respect and commitment to the autonomy of the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 He assured that his government would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so that the weight would be artificially strengthened.\par \par \uc2 The market should be regulated with the market, no \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionism\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Not that it's the first time he's said it, but it's important when he repeats it.\par \par \uc2 And among bankers, the issues of financial inclusion and digital modernization of banking, although discussed, were overtaken by the central theme, the challenge posed by the global double crisis: the price war on the oil market and the impact coronavirus, whose impacts were reflected by the pair of black days observed on 9 and 12 March.\par \par \uc2 For H\u233\'00\'E9ctor Grisi, the CEO of Santander Mexico, both crises can become an opportunity for the country.\par \par \uc2 Taking the right public policies Mexico could increase its trade importance with the US, in view of China's coronavirus involvement.\par \par \uc2 The reorientation of the current government's energy policy would be strategic, said Barclays Mexico's president and CEO, RaulMart\u237\'00\'EDnez Ostos. From its point of view, the current government is very clear that it must open up the energy sector to domestic and international private investment.In the banking run, managers agree that Mexico is facing a double crisis and an opportunity. Show me.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200313eg3d002jv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
