\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's peso firms as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  boosts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Oktober 2017\par 00:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso strengthened\par on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to cushion the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent decline, lifting it from six-month lows.\par     The peso firmed 0.99 percent, making it the top\par gainer among \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region and paring its losses this\par month to around 4 percent.\par     Mexico's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commission said on Wednesday it would\par increase the amount of dollars auctioned in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par hedges following a period of market volatility.\par     Strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was\par meant to curb price pressures stemming from a weaker peso, which\par could delay policymaker efforts to slow down inflation.\par     Concerns over the future of Mexico's trade ties with the\par United States have hammered the peso in recent weeks as fears\par grew that U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  could make good on his\par threats to scrap the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North American Free Trade Agreement\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \uc2 \f2 NAFTA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ).\par     The Mexican stock exchange closed down 2.55 percent as\par shares of \f28 \uc2 \f2 America Movil\f28 \uc2 \f2  fell as much as 6.93 percent.\par On Tuesday, the telecoms firm reported a net loss of 9.55\par billion pesos ($501.63 million) for the third quarter, hit by a\par costly Colombian arbitration panel ruling.\par     Brazilian markets seesawed on Wednesday, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  up 0.32 percent and stocks up 0.42 percent.\par     Traders mostly avoided making big bets ahead of a widely\par expected lower house vote on whether to put President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michel\par Temer\f28 \uc2 \f2  on trial in the Supreme Court for corruption charges.\par     Investors largely bet he will dodge the charges, but a\par smaller show of support could further delay his efforts to\par streamline the costly social security system, which are seen as\par critical to boosting long-term economic growth.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2010 GMT:\par     \par  Stock indexes                                 daily %      YTD %\par                                 Latest          change     change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets              1113.49       0.02      29.12\par                                                         \par  MSCI LatAm                         2887.35       0.16      23.16\par                                                         \par  Brazil Bovespa                    76671.13       0.42      27.30\par  Mexico IPC                        48876.46      -2.55       7.08\par  Chile IPSA                         5495.09      -0.74      32.37\par                                                         \par  Chile IGPA                        27566.78      -0.66      32.95\par  Argentina MerVal                  27865.83      -0.51      64.71\par                                                         \par  Colombia IGBC                     10956.49       0.77       8.18\par                                           