\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's peso rebounds as cenbank steps up  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2017\par 18:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Recasts, adds analyst's comments)\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 MEXICO\b0 \highlight\uc2  CITY, Oct 25 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso snapped back on Wednesday, gaining as much as 1.3 percent, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would accelerate its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a bid to stem the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent fall to six-month lows against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The peso has been on a roller coaster ride this year due to uncertainty over negotiations to update the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2  (\uc2 NAFTA\uc2 ), a lynchpin of Mexico's economy.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has threatened to tear up the 23-year-old accord, which underpins $1.3 trillion in annual trade between Canada, the United States and Mexico, if it cannot be reworked to benefit U.S. jobs and reduce the trade deficit.\par \par \uc2 After slipping to an all-time low of 22.04 to the dollar in early January, a rosier outlook for \uc2 NAFTA\uc2  helped the peso steadily gain to 17.47 by July 18, making it the best performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world over the period.\par \par \uc2 But amid renewed uncertainty over the trade talks pushing the peso to six-month lows, Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  commission said on Wednesday it will raise the amount of dollars auctioned in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hedges.\par \par \uc2 In a statement issued by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the commission said it would raise the amount regularly auctioned from a pool of $20 billion set aside for the purpose in February.\par \par \uc2 "Past form suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions should provide some relief for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but that this could be fleeting," Neil Shearing, chief emerging markets economist at Capital Economics, said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 "The prospects for the peso over the next couple of months will be determined by whether \uc2 NAFTA\uc2  talks can get back on track. We're increasingly concerned," Shearing added.\par \par \uc2 So far, Mexico has auctioned $1 billion in hedges from the pool in lots of $200 million. It will now offer another $4 billion through Dec. 6. in larger amounts, starting with an auction of $1 billion on Thursday, the commission said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will hold three auctions on Oct. 26 for a total of $1 billion worth of peso hedging instruments due to expire in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 The auctions comprise a 32-day instrument worth $400 million expiring on Nov. 27, a 61-day instrument worth $300 million expiring on Dec. 26, and a 90-day instrument worth $300 million expiring on Jan. 24, 2018. (Reporting by \uc2 Miguel Gutierrez\uc2  and Anthony Esposito; editing by Susan Thomas) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-10-25T17:32:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020171025edap00oe1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
