\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2 's peso firms as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  boosts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Oktober 2017\par 17:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, Oct 25 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso strengthened\par on Wednesday after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in to cushion the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent decline, lifting it from six-month lows.\par     The peso firmed 0.9 percent, making it the top\par gainer among \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region and paring its losses this\par month to around 4 percent.\par     Mexico's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  commission said on Wednesday it would\par increase the amount of dollars auctioned in foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par hedges following a period of market volatility.\par     Strategists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  conjectured that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par was meant to curb price pressures stemming from a weaker peso,\par which could delay policymaker efforts to slow down inflation.\par     Concerns over the future of Mexico's trade ties with the\par United States have hammered the peso in recent weeks as fears\par grew that U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  could make good on his\par threats to scrap the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North American Free Trade Agreement\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par (\f28 \uc2 \f2 NAFTA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ).\par     Brazilian markets seesawed on Wednesday, with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  up 0.2 percent and stocks down by the same amount.\par     Traders mostly avoided making big bets ahead of a\par widely-expected lower house vote on whether to put President\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Michel Temer\f28 \uc2 \f2  on trial in the Supreme Court for corruption\par charges.\par     Investors largely bet he will dodge the charges, but a\par smaller show of support could further delay his efforts to\par streamline the costly social security system, which are seen as\par critical to boosting long-term economic growth.\par     Shares in retailer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lojas Renner SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  and motor\par maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 WEG SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  rose, however, after posting their\par third-quarter earnings. Despite missing expectations for net\par income, a 15 percent annual increase in WEG's operating profits\par supported demand for the stock.\par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1500 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                                daily %    YTD %\par                                                change   change\par                                    Latest              \par  MSCI Emerging Markets              1115.07      0.16    29.12\par  MSCI LatAm                         2882.61         0    23.16\par  Brazil Bovespa                    76164.29     -0.24    26.46\par  Mexico S&P/BVM IPC                49471.17     -1.37     8.39\par  Chile IPSA                         5515.08     -0.38    32.85\par  Chile IGPA                        27654.63     -0.34    33.38\par  Argentina MerVal                  27710.39     -1.07    63.79\par  Colombia IGBC                     10918.60      0.42     7.81\par  Venezuela IBC                       683.83      2.99   -97.84\par                                                               \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                    daily %    YTD %\par         