\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso gains on  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention \highlight\uc2  as Fed eyed\b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 April 2017\par 18:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, April 5 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso led gains\par among Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday, supported by\par market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of the release of\par the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy meeting minutes.\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banco de Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2  fully rolled over $500 million worth of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging instruments originally sold a month ago to stem\par a slump in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The peso is now up 11 percent so far this year, rebounding\par from all-time lows in 2016 amid fresh hopes that U.S. President\par Donald Trump will not impose heavy tariffs on Mexican exports to\par the United States as he had threatened.\par     The peso firmed nearly 0.5 percent on Thursday,\par while other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the region were mostly flat.\par     Traders avoided big bets before the release of the U.S.\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  March policy meeting minutes later in the day.\par     Investors have closely monitored the Fed's communication in\par search of hints over when U.S. interest rates will rise again,\par potentially draining capital away from higher-yielding emerging\par markets.\par     U.S. companies hired the most workers in over two years in\par March, supporting the Fed's view for at least two more hikes by\par year-end.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1610 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                     Latest       Daily     YTD\par                                                   pct     pct\par                                                change  change\par  MSCI Emerging Markets                970.16     0.52   11.93\par  MSCI LatAm                         2,690.27     0.79   14.03\par  Brazil Bovespa                    65,655.72    -0.17    9.01\par  Mexico IPC                        49,227.97    -0.23    7.85\par  Chile IPSA                         4,857.06     0.65   17.00\par  Chile IGPA                        24,297.86     0.58   17.19\par  Argentina MerVal                  20,836.01        0   23.16\par  Colombia IGBC                     10,223.33     0.42    0.94\par  Venezuela IBC                     45,184.30    -1.21   42.51\par                                                              \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Latest    Daily     YTD\par                                                   pct     pct\par                                                change  change\par  Brazil real                          3.0914     0.19    5.10\par  Mexico peso                         18.7300     0.47   10.75\par  Chile peso                            658.5     0.29    1.85\par  Colombia peso                      2,857.83     0.12    5.03\par  Peru sol                              3.248     0.06    5.11\par  Argentina peso (interbank)          15.3575    -0.02    3.37\par                                                        \par  Argentina peso (parallel)             15.79     0.57    6.52\par                                                        \par  \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski,