\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso pares losses ahead of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2017\par 22:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, April 4 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso pared losses\par on Tuesday after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced it would\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in an effort to ease\par pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexico's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would sell up to $200 million\par worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging instruments to roll over paper set to\par expire on Wednesday, just ahead of a meeting between U.S.\par President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Chinese President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The bank had originally issued the instruments as a way to\par stem the peso's slide following the election of Trump, who\par threatened to scrap trade agreements with Mexico.\par     The peso has since made up some lost ground as those\par concerns eased, with investors betting that he would not impose\par big tariffs on Mexican exports to the United States.\par     Still, the peso fell the most among Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , weakening more than 0.8 percent.\par     Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell ahead of the Xi meeting,\par which Trump has said "will be a very difficult one." He has held\par out the possibility of using trade as a lever to secure China's\par cooperation against North Korea.\par     Stock markets in the region were largely buoyant.\par     Argentina's benchmark stock index rose about 0.9\par percent, touching a record high for the sixth straight trading\par day, after agency S&P raised the country's sovereign rating by a\par notch to B from B-.\par         \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2020 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                    Latest        Daily  YTD pct\par                                                   pct   change\par                                                change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                965.17     0.02    11.93\par  MSCI LatAm                         2,669.06     0.44    14.03\par  Brazil Bovespa                    65,768.91     0.85     9.20\par  Mexico IPC                        49,342.77     1.07     8.11\par  Chile IPSA                         4,825.76     0.71    16.24\par  Chile IGPA                        24,158.32      0.6    16.51\par  Argentina MerVal                  20,744.08     0.88    22.62\par  Colombia IGBC                     10,180.99     0.07     0.52\par  Venezuela IBC                     45,739.70     3.99    44.27\par                                                               \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                                   pct   change\par                                                change  \par  Brazil real                          3.0978     0.55     4.89\par  Mexico peso                         18.8305    -0.85    10.16\par  Chile peso                            660.4    -0.33     1.56\par  Colombia peso                       2,865.2     0.00     4.76\par  Peru sol                               3.25     0.00    