\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso pares losses ahead of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 434 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2017\par 19:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, April 4 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso pared losses\par on Tuesday after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced it would\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in an effort to ease\par pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it would sell up to $200\par million worth of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedging instruments to roll over\par papers set to expire on Wednesday, just ahead of a meeting\par between U.S. President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Chinese President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Xi\par Jinping\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The bank had originally issued the instruments as a way to\par stem the peso's slide following the U.S. election of Trump, who\par pledged to scrap trade agreements with Mexico.\par     The peso has since rebounded as those concerns eased, with\par investors betting that he would not impose big tariffs on\par Mexican exports to the United States.\par     Still, it remained the biggest decliner among Latin American\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , weakening nearly 1 percent following a 10 percent\par increase so far this year.\par     Most Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  slipped ahead of Trump's\par meeting with Xi, which Trump has said "will be a very difficult\par one." He has held out the possibility of using trade as a lever\par to secure China's cooperation against North Korea at the\par Thursday-Friday meeting.\par     Argentina's benchmark stock index rose 0.7 percent,\par touching a record high for the sixth straight trading day, after\par agency S&P raised the country's sovereign rating by a notch to B\par from B-.\par         \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1715 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                    Latest        Daily  YTD pct\par                                                   pct   change\par                                                change  \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                963.58    -0.16    11.93\par  MSCI LatAm                         2,661.99     0.17    13.54\par  Brazil Bovespa                    65,469.14      0.4     8.70\par  Mexico IPC                        49,165.72     0.71     7.72\par  Chile IPSA                         4,801.89     0.22    15.67\par  Chile IGPA                        24,051.51     0.16    16.00\par  Argentina MerVal                  20,713.12     0.73    22.43\par  Colombia IGBC                     10,155.24    -0.18     0.27\par  Venezuela IBC                     45,739.70     3.99    44.27\par                                                               \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                            Latest    Daily  YTD pct\par                                                   pct   change\par                                                change  \par  Brazil real                          3.1180    -0.16     4.21\par  Mexico peso                         18.8355    -0.87    10.13\par  Chile peso                            660.4    -0.33     1.56\par  Colombia peso                         2,867    -0.06     4.69\par  Peru sol                               3.2