\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  peso dips even as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 345 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2017\par 22:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  (Updates table)\par     SAO PAULO, March 6 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso weakened\par slightly on Monday even after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par support the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold $1 billion worth of a new peso hedge\par instrument similar to non-deliverable forwards. Total demand for\par the new instruments was $2.075 billion, the bank said.\par \par     It had announced last month that it would sell up to $20\par billion in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hedges to shore up the peso, which has been\par battered by U.S. President Donald Trump's pledges to tear up the\par North America Free Trade Agreement (\f28 \uc2 \f2 NAFTA\f28 \uc2 \f2 ).\par     Still, the peso has rebounded in recent weeks on\par hopes that the United States and Mexico could strike a mutually\par beneficial deal.\par     It hit a nearly four-month high on Monday, extending gains\par from last week triggered by comments from a high-ranking U.S.\par trade official, before turning lower.\par     Other Latin American \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were down as riskier assets\par slipped around the world.\par     The Brazilian real weakened 0.3 percent, while the\par country's benchmark Bovespa stock index fell 0.9\par percent. \par \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2100 GMT:\par  Stock