\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Turkey's  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  war-chest - $100 bln or a third of that?\b0\par\par\uc2 702 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2017\par 10:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats from Tuesday without changes)\par \par \uc2 By Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 10 (Reuters) - As the peso plunged last week, \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dug deep to sell more than $1 billion on Asian, European and U.S. markets. But Turkey, facing a similar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selloff, lacks the luxury of a war-chest it could raid to stabilise the lira.\par \par \uc2 With the lira plumbing new record lows to be 2017's worst performing big emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, analysts reckon raising interest rates is the only option for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the government is firmly opposed to a move that would harm economic growth.\par \par \uc2 On the face of it, Turkey's hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves look healthy - \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed total reserves of around $106 billion at the end of 2016. But $14 billion of that was gold and a further breakdown of the total figure shows a less rosy picture - especially when contrasted with the amount of external debt that must be repaid in coming months.\par \par \uc2 Calculations from \uc2 UBS\uc2  and other banks in London and Istanbul, based on data from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , estimate the true level of usable reserves at closer to $35 billion.\par \par \uc2 "Strictly speaking, a lot of the money is not deployable by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  ... A lot of it is commercial bank reserves deposited at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," \uc2 UBS\uc2  strategist Manik Narain said.\par \par \uc2 He calculates that $42 billion is made up of Turkish banks' mandatory hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve deposits with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offset their dollar lending within the country.\par \par \uc2 And another $16 billion is accounted for by the "reserves option mechanism", which allows banks to hold part of their lira reserves in hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  RESERVES\par \par \uc2 "So when the heat turns up, they have to resort to a conventional interest rate defence because by any metric they have among the lowest reserve adequacy levels in emerging markets ... They will inspire a lot of market concern if they deplete reserves too aggressively," Narain added.\par \par \uc2 Whether reserves are adequate can be gauged in several ways. One is the number of months of imports the reserves will buy, with three months deemed to be the safe minimum.\par \par \uc2 Calculations by \uc2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\uc2  (BAML) show Turkey can fund 5.6 months of imports if a reserve level of nearly $100 billion is assumed.\par \par \uc2 The second method, based on the so-called Guidotti-Greenspan rule, requires reserves to be at least equal to foreign debt payments in the coming year. The rationale is that countries should have sufficient buffers to resist a sudden halt in external financing.\par \par \uc2 BAML estimated total Turkish external debt at $421 billion, with $107.3 billion due in the coming year. The latter would be more or less on par with headline reserves, but three times more than "usable" levels.\par \par \uc2 By that yardstick, Turkey's reserve adequacy would be below that of countries such as Egypt or Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Other analysts point out that, while Turkey may not have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, it has been steadily releasing dollars into the market.\par \par \uc2 HSBC\uc2  strategist Murat Toprak said the steady decline in reserves - buffers fell by $6 billion between November-December - should be seen in the light of cuts in banks' hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve requirements. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  cut the rate again this week, estimating this would inject $1.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 "So in a way the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using its reserves to inject dollar liquidity into the system," Toprak said.\par \par \uc2 "We can't say for sure they will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets because of current reserve levels but obviously they have limited ammunition."\par \par \uc2 In any case, the effects of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are usually short-lived. Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent huge dollar sale, the peso fell back to record lows on Friday, suggesting Turkey may be better off resorting to a big interest rate rise.\par \par \uc2 However, President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  and his advisers have repeatedly called for lower rates to stimulate economic growth, with some even suggesting that raising borrowing costs would amount to plotting against the state. (Reporting by Sujata Rao; Editing by Gareth Jones) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-1-11T10:28:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170111ed1b00efj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
