\par\par \b \uc2 Global Equities Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,336 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2017\par 23:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 17:09 ET - The peso gained from the previous day but posted a 2.6% loss in a volatile week that saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit new lows and then rebound thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar was quoted in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  City at MXN21.2470 compared with MX21.4535 Thursday. The benchmark IPC stock index fell 1.4% to 46,072, ending a string of four straight wins. Among the few gainers were \uc2 Grupo Carso\uc2  (GCARSO.MX) and \uc2 Empresas ICA\uc2  (ICA.MX)--up 2.2% and 17%, respectively--which form part of a consortium that won a $4B contract to build the new Mexico City airport terminal. (anthony.harrup@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:58 ET - Private-equity firm \uc2 Pamplona Capital Management\uc2 , which acquired \uc2 MedAssets\uc2  in January 2016 for about $2B, announces a joint venture to manage physician practices and medical groups' billing and collection efforts. The joint venture with \uc2 Northwell Health\uc2 , a hospital operator based in Great Neck, N.Y., will market consulting, scheduling and billing and collection services to physician practices, the companies say. Pamplona acquired a large healthcare billing and collection business with its \uc2 MedAssets\uc2  acquisition. \uc2 Northwell Health\uc2 , which also owns an insurance company, will be among the clients of the joint venture, called Formativ Health. (melanie.evans@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:47 ET - Another retailer reports poor holiday sales and warns about 4Q as it cuts yearly guidance. \uc2 Stage Stores\uc2  (SSI), a specialty department store chain, says \uc2 SSS\uc2  decline 7.3% for the holiday period. The shortfall has SSI lowering 4Q EPS to 20c-35c versus its prior 65c-90c view. For the full-year, SSI now sees a loss of 70-85 cents-a-share versus the 15-40 cents-a-share yearly loss it originally projected. "Holiday comparable sales were below our expectations and increased promotions significantly pressured gross margin," CEO \uc2 Michael Glazer\uc2  says. SSI's bad news is the latest in a series of retail warnings this week that included \uc2 Macy's\uc2  (M), \uc2 Kohl's\uc2  (KSS), Victoria's Secret owner \uc2 L Brands\uc2  (LB), and others. SSI is off 12% to $3.50 after-hours. (patrick.sheridan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 16:06 ET - Dow Jones Industrial Average comes within 0.37 point of the 20,000 milestone, but fails to break above that level on a day where the other two major averages close at new highs. December payroll additions were slightly below expectations, while wage figures suggest higher inflation may be on the horizon. DJIA gains 64 points to 19963, the S&P 500 rises 7 to 2276 and the \uc2 Nasdaq\uc2  climbs 33 to 5521, extending its New Year's winning streak. Treasury prices pull back, with the 10-year yield rising to 2.42%, while a stronger dollar weighs on oil and gold prices. (patrick.sullivan@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:39 ET - \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Chicago\uc2  head \uc2 Charles Evans\uc2  said on CNBC he was untroubled by the current level of the stock market. Given that the "fundamentals for 2017 look pretty good," Evans said it "makes sense" to see the stock market around its current levels. The Dow Jones Industrial Average has been flirting with achieving the landmark 20,000 reading over recent days. Evans also reiterated that he believes the Fed could raise rates two to three times in 2017. (michael.derby@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:27 ET - \uc2 The Consumer Financial Protection Bureau\uc2  filled several senior leadership positions as it prepares for the arrival of a new Republican administration that could bring fundamental changes to its structure and \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The agency has named Leandra English, a former \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  official returning to the bureau, as its new Chief of Staff. She will be assisting Director \uc2 Richard Cordray\uc2 , who is in the cross hairs of Republican lawmakers vying to potentially weaken the CFPB under the Trump presidency. Being promoted internally is Elizabeth Reilly, who will serve as Chief Financial Officer. Two Assistant Directors were also appointed. (yuka.hayashi@wsj.com; @TokyoWoods)\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 15:12 ET - The \uc2 CBOE\uc2  Volatility Index (VIX) is down nearly 19% in just the first four trading sessions of the year, trading at around 11.42 Friday afternoon after finishing last year at 14.04. That means the index, which investors use to measure expectations for stock swings in the next 30 days, is on pace for its second-largest drop at the start of a year. The only year the VIX fared worse in its first four sessions of trade was 2013, when it fell 23%, according to the WSJ Market Data Group. (akane.otani@wsj.com; @akaneotani)\par \par \uc2 15:02 ET - Not everyone got gold wrong in 2016. UBS analyst Joni Teves walked away with a pair of one ounce gold bars after winning two categories of the LBMA's contest for forecasting precious metals prices. The average price of gold in 2016 was $1,251 a troy ounce, not far from Ms. Teves' forecast of $1,225 a troy ounce. She also took first place for her silver outlook: silver finished the year with a $17.14 average price, compared to Teves' forecast of an average price of $17.20 a troy ounce. George Coles of Metals Focus got the prize for platinum. The palladium forecasting prize went to Bernard Dahdah of \uc2 Natixis\uc2 . (ira.iosebashvili@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 14:43 ET - The Dow's rapid rise is good news for South Florida residential real estate broker Michelle Farber Ross. "People are looking at their net worth and feeling more confident," she says. About five prospective buyers a week are doing walk-in tours of the luxury homes and investment properties Ross sells. Last year around this time, she had only one walk-in a week. She also just got an offer for a $12M investment property in the Bahamas she listed nine months ago. If the Dow hits 20K, she expects even more interest from domestic buyers. Her foreign clients aren't feeling as good though. "They're waiting to see what happens with immigration and trade." (Veronica.Dagher@wsj.com; @VeronicaDagher)\par \par \uc2 14:29 ET - The Lollapalooza of health-care investing gets underway this weekend: the \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  conference that draws thousands of investors and industry executives to San Francisco each January. One of the hosts, JPMorgan drug-stock analyst Chris Schott, says it comes on the heels of "a challenging 2016 that saw a sharp increase in drug price scrutiny and deteriorating specialty pharma fundamentals." He says specialty pharma companies like \uc2 Perrigo\uc2  (PRGO) and Teva (TEVA) could have another tough year on generic-drug pricing pressure, but sentiment on major pharma stocks like \uc2 Eli Lilly\uc2  (LLY) and \uc2 Bristol-Myers\uc2  (BMY) is improving on solid expectations for new products. (peter.loftus@wsj.com; @Loftus)\par \par \uc2 14:22 ET - \uc2 Facebook\uc2  (FB) has hired Campbell Brown, a former anchor for \uc2 CNN\uc2  and NBC, to run news partnerships. Brown will pitch and solicit publishers' feedback on products like Instant Articles and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  Live, but she won't decide how FB should handle sensitive and newsworthy content, like the 30-minute live video posted this week showing a Chicago man being tortured. FB has a wary relationship with media outlets. FB's dominance in digital ads has hurt the economics of many publishers. Users and media outlets have also criticized FB for allowing the spread of fake news on its platform in recent months. (deepa.seetharaman@wsj.com; @dseetharaman)\par \par \uc2 14:18 ET - \uc2 Neiman Marcus\uc2  withdraws plans for an IPO, amid a rough stretch for retailers, with \uc2 Macy's\uc2  (M) and \uc2 Sears\uc2  (SHLD) announcing store closures and slumping sales. The move raises questions about the upscale department-store chain's future and how investors \uc2 Ares Management\uc2  (ARES) and \uc2 Canada Pension Plan Investment Board\uc2  will exit their 2013 $6B buyout of it. \uc2 Neiman Marcus\uc2  didn't detail why it's shelving plans for a listing in a regulatory filing. (matthew.jarzemsky@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 January 06, 2017 17:09 ET (22:09 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170106ed16003mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
