\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Mexico \highlight\uc2  cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to prop peso, fend off life lows\b0\par\par\uc2 439 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2017\par 23:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Updates prices)\par     SAO PAULO, Jan 5 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso strengthened\par slightly on Thursday in a day of volatile trading after the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold dollars to support the ailing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which\par has been battered by uncertainty over U.S. President-elect\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     The peso firmed 0.13 percent to 21.4225 per dollar\par following the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a day after the slumping \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par hit a record low. \par     Traders said the bank sold $1 billion in New York and Mexico\par in its first such move since February 2016. Mexican financial\par authorities were mum on the amount, but said they could not rule\par out further discretionary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to staunch the bleeding. \par     Analysts with \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  praised the move, saying the bank\par will need to adopt a more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy than it\par did in the last two years in order to correct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par imbalances.\par     In a client note, they estimated the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mexican \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par currently has more than $40 billion on hand it could use to\par buffer the peso's decline.\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  posted its worst yearly performance since 2008\par last year on concerns that Trump could enact protectionist\par policies against Mexico.\par     It extended losses in the first days of 2017 after carmaker\par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Ford Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2  announced it would cancel a planned $1.6\par billion investment in central Mexico following criticism by\par Trump. \par     The peso fell again on Thursday afternoon when Trump\par threatened a hefty tax for Toyota if it builds its Corolla cars\par for the U.S. market at a plant in Mexico before\par rebounding slightly.   \par     \par     Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 2200 GMT:\par     \par  Stock                                    Latest    daily % change  YTD % change\par    indexes                                                          \par  MSCI Emerging Markets                    881.72    1.18            2.26\par                                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                               2403.05   0.98            2.67\par                                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                           62070.98  0.78            3.06\par  Mexico IPC                               46719.99  0.28            2.36\par  Chile IPSA                               4163.65   -0.11           0.30\par  Chile IGPA                               20785.21  -0.12           0.25\par  Argentina MerVal                         18222.70  0.43            7.71\par  Colombia IGBC                            10317.51  0.28            1.87\par  Venezuela IBC                            32611.87  2.43            2.86\par                                                                     \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                Latest    daily % change  YTD % change\par  Brazil real                              3.1990    -0.08           1.57\par  Mexico peso                              21.4350   0.07            -3.22\par  Chile peso                               661.6     0.00            1.38\par  Colombia peso                            2930.51   1.31            2.42\par                                                                     \par  Peru sol                                 3.364     0.00            1.49\par  Argentina peso (interbank)               15.9550   0.88            -0.50\par                                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)                16.82     0.83            0.00\par                                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski; Editing by Nick Zieminski and\par Grant McCool)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-1-5T23:36:51.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170105ed15016wj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
