\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico seen making big rate hike to defend peso if Trump wins\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2016\par 07:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (Reuters) - \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen raising its key interest rate by at least 75 basis points on Wednesday if U.S. Republican candidate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wins the U.S. election to become the country's next president, three economists said.\par \par \uc2 Trump, who has threatened to rip up the \uc2 North American Free Trade Agreement\uc2  and build a wall between Mexico and the U.S. border, was leading the vote against Democratic rival \uc2 Hillary Clinton\uc2 , according to media projections.\par \par \uc2 Trump's lead pushed the peso to a record low, falling around 13 percent and breaking the 20 pesos-per-dollar barrier in its biggest fall since the 1994 Tequila Crisis.\par \par \uc2 Three economists told Reuters they expected the \uc2 Banco de Mexico\uc2  to raise its benchmark interest rate by between 75 and 150 basis points in an extraordinary meeting on Wednesday if Trump wins. One of them said the bank could opt for a swap with the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  depending how the peso evolves.\par \par \uc2 "It is going to be quite difficult to navigate through this," said Carlos Serrano, an economist at Bancomer in Mexico City. He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to act swiftly.\par \par \uc2 Serrano thought an emergency hike of at least 100 basis points was needed to help calm markets. If foreign investors start to dump peso-denominated bonds in a stampede for the exits, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could hike again, he said.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso had already been one of the worst performing major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has hiked interest rates three times this year in a bid to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and keep its weakness from driving up inflation.\par \par \uc2 The bank last moved in September, when it raised its benchmark rate <MXCBIR=ECI> 50 basis points to 4.75 percent, its highest level since the crisis year of 2009, when the Mexican economy was mired in the global economic crisis.\par \par \uc2 Interest rate increases and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market have been \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main tools to support the peso, which is down around 18 percent so far this year.\par \par \uc2 The bank was next scheduled to meet to discuss rates on November 17.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  usually only changes its benchmark rate at scheduled policy meetings. In February, it acted without announcing it was having a meeting after a deep peso slump.\par \par \uc2 Gabriel Casillas\uc2 , an economist at Banorte, said the peso could suffer for months as the market tries to figure out what Trump could do in office.\par \par \uc2 \u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0"The worst part will be when we know the results and before the inauguration. Because of the uncertainty of what Trump could do, consumers will postpone purchases, companies will postpone investments," Casillas said.\par \par \uc2 \u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0Casillas thinks a Trump victory could shave up to 0.3 percentage points off Mexico's gross domestic product this year. But things could look up once Trump is in office and he finds it harder than expected to unwind free trade with Mexico.\par \par \uc2 \u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0\u160\'00\'A0"I don't think Trump will do a lot of the things he said he will do," he said.\par \par \uc2 (Writing by Gabriel Stargardter; Editing by Simon Gardner and Mary Milliken) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-11-9T06:29:12.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020161109ecb900911\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
