\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam stocks,  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  up ahead of British referendum\b0\par\par\uc2 447 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2016\par 23:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (Adds Colombia, analyst comment on Mexico, updates prices)\par     By Bruno Federowski\par     SAO PAULO, June 22 (Reuters) - Most Latin American stocks\par and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rose on Wednesday as optimism grew that Britain\par would vote to remain in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  a day before the\par closely watched referendum.\par     The Mexican peso  strengthened for a fourth\par consecutive day, sidestepping a drop in crude prices. The peso\par in Colombia jumped 1.9 percent to its highest in two\par weeks.\par     Betting markets have shown bigger chances of a "Remain"\par victory, though opinion polls have generally indicated a tight\par race. Investors worry a possible "Brexit" could disrupt\par financial markets and weigh on global risk appetite.\par     Mexico's peso had weakened to a four-month low last week,\par nearing levels which last triggered direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Mexico\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , Latin America's second-biggest\par economy, is often used as a proxy for traders taking short\par positions in other emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and could suffer most in\par the region if Britain votes to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\par     "Despite the recent reiteration of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2 's hawkish bias,\par we consider the (Mexican peso) as the most vulnerable in (Latin\par America) to a flare-up in global macro risks," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 \par emerging market strategists said in a note.\par     On Tuesday, a board member from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Mexico\f28 \uc2 \f2  flagged\par the recent slump in the peso as the biggest risk to Mexico's\par efforts to meet its inflation target. \par     Brazil's benchmark Bovespa stock index fell 1.2\par percent after rising 4.6 percent over five consecutive positive\par sessions.\par     \par     Key Latin American stock indexes and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at 1956 GMT:\par  Stock indexes                             daily %     YTD %\par                                Latest       change    change\par  \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  Emerging Markets            830.86      0.67      3.93\par                                                     \par  MSCI LatAm                      2166.91      0.23     18.15\par                                                     \par  Brazil Bovespa                 50228.74      -1.2     15.87\par                                                     \par  Mexico IPC                     45802.81      0.21      6.57\par                                                     \par  Chile IPSA                      3994.67      0.14      8.54\par                                                     \par  Chile IGPA                     19736.48      0.12      8.73\par                                                     \par  Argentina MerVal               13757.43      0.55     17.83\par                                                     \par  Colombia IGBC                   9874.35     -0.12     15.53\par                                                     \par  Venezuela IBC                  13957.46     -0.76     -4.32\par                                                     \par                                                             \par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                                 daily %     YTD %\par                                             change    change\par                                   Latest            \par  Brazil real                      3.3780      0.80     14.42\par                                                     \par  Mexico peso                     18.5015      0.66     -7.38\par                                                     \par  Chile peso                       674.23      0.20      5.00\par                                                     \par  Colombia peso                      2918      1.89      7.93\par                                                     \par  Peru sol                          3.286      0.03      3.75\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (interbank)      14.0700     -0.72     -8.38\par                                                     \par  Argentina peso (parallel)         14.51     -0.35     -1.68\par                                                     \par  \par  (Reporting by Bruno Federowski, additional reporting by Michael\par O'Boyle and Anna Yukhananov; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama and Diane\par Craft)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-22T22:01:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160622ec6m01xwt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
