\par\par \b \uc2 Mexico peso sinks to lowest since rate hike in Feb\b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Juni 2016\par 15:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, June 13 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso tumbled on Monday to its weakest in nearly four months, sinking for the third session in a row and trading around levels last seen when Mexico used a surprise interest rate hike to defend its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The peso sank nearly 0.8 percent to 18.78 per dollar, its weakest since Feb. 17, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made an unscheduled rate decision and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since 2009.\par \par \uc2 The peso has shed about 3.5 percent in the last three sessions as concerns that Britain could leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  rocked riskier assets around the world. (Reporting by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-13T14:26:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160613ec6d014tm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
