\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Mexico's Carstens sees no peso attack, as bets recede on rate hike\b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2016\par 04:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds Carstens comment on local radio)               \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, May 25 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso is not seeing a new speculative attack despite its recent slump, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Agustin Carstens\uc2  said on Wednesday, prompting investors to cut back bets on an aggressive Mexican interest rate hike.               \par \par \uc2 A tumble in the peso in May has stoked expectations that Mexico could raise interest rates next month in a bid to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 But Carstens said the peso's depreciation had not been driven by any specific bet against the peso, which has weakened  along with other emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this month.               \par \par \uc2 "We certainly are not seeing a speculative attack," Carstens told a conference in Mexico City about the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's quarterly inflation report.               \par \par \uc2 His comments fed expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not close to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets anytime soon.               \par \par \uc2 Yields on Mexican interest rate swaps fell after Carstens' comments, as investors dialed back expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would hike its benchmark interest rate at the next meeting in late June.               \par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso has slumped about 7 percent this month, the second-worst performer among the world's 36 most-traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , behind the South African rand.               \par \par \uc2 A sharp drop in \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2 's peso pushed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in February to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets for the first time since 2009 and to raise interest rates unexpectedly after an unannounced meeting.               \par \par \uc2 Mexican policymakers said then the peso was being targeted by electronic trading programs, and cited the relatively sound position of the economy.               \par \par \uc2 Carstens said \b \highlight22\uc2 Mexico\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not ruled out \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  again under exceptional circumstances.               \par \par \uc2 According to a Reuters poll taken earlier on Wednesday, a majority of economists thought it was unlikely \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would make another unexpected rate hike in a bid to support the peso and they saw less than a 50 percent chance of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .               \par \par \uc2 In an interview on local radio on Wednesday evening, Carstens said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be "very attentive" to the relative monetary policy between the United States and Mexico.               \par \par \uc2 "In the event that there is movement from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the United States, it is feasible that we might have to react also," he said.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  maintained its 2016 economic growth forecast at between 2.0 and 3.0 percent, but trimmed its view for 2017 to between 2.3 and 3.3 percent because of weakness in U.S. industrial output, Carstens said during the conference.               